    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, but the outlook is anchored by two high-upside plays against favorable matchups. **Kyle Tucker** (85.72) and **Andy Pages** (75.63) are our strongest starts, both drawing a prime target in Sugano (xERA 4.93). **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite status remains unchallenged, bolstered by an excellent 19% boost from the SP skill profile and park factors. **Andy Pages** is similarly positioned for a productive afternoon; his score is elevated by an aggressive +14% park adjustment and the SP advantage, cementing him as a core building block. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (72.04) surprises as a top-tier play due to his leadoff role (+10%) and his robust 0.373 xwOBA, providing significant leverage against Ober.\n\nThe middle of the order faces tighter windows. **Gunnar Henderson** (51.50) and **Coby Mayo** (53.64) draw a difficult assignment in McClanahan (xERA 4.14), which suppressed their ceilings despite their talent. **Gunnar Henderson** specifically sees a 15% hit due to the L/L platoon disadvantage, and we will monitor his performance closely to see if he can overcome the inefficiency. The most difficult decision today was at the margins, where **Sam Antonacci** (39.73) fell just shy of the starting threshold. While his park factors and recency are solid, his position in the seven-hole and a negative platoon split against Imanaga dropped him below our 40.0 floor, prioritizing our preservation of game caps over a marginal start. We remain cautious with **Liam Hicks**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as all four hover in the low 50s, requiring efficient at-bats to justify their inclusion over the bench. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently on the IL, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** observing a team off-day, our depth is strained, leaving little room for error if weather or late lineup shifts impact our core contributors.",
